it is so peaceful and beautiful that  it's hard to imagine anything horrible  happening here  but it did and the effects still  reverberate  september 2012 saddam hilly and his  family leave surrey and come to anisee  on holiday they camp they swim and then  one day  mother father and grandmother are all  shot dead on a quiet woodland road along  with a french cyclist  the police arrived to find a hellish  scene  bodies and bullet casings the family car  reversed into an earth bank in an effort  to escape but there was nothing here to  identify the killer  the family's two young daughters  survived one stumbling around badly  injured the other hiding in the car  under a body  the police investigation grew and grew  mr al hilly's brother was arrested and  then let go and a hunt was launched for  this man a motorcyclist spotted near the  scene  he was eventually found questioned and  released  but earlier this week the same man was  arrested once more raising hopes of a  breakthrough instead he was released  again  and so the specter of unsolved murder  still lingers over this area and its  people what uh  when i saw that a man had been arrested  i was reassured and i thought it could  be him and this case could finally be  solved and now we're back to square one  with a family who'll never know if  anyone will be arrested and found guilty  for these deaths  well nine years ago the villager was in  total shock when we learned that there  had been four murders so it did create  hysteria and mayhem in the village  the hysteria has eased  life has gone back to normal except that  here  everybody knows about the killings  anisee is a popular tourist destination  but this is a pretty remote corner and  as the family drove up the road on a  late summer's afternoon they only seem  to have passed a few people on bicycles  now what happened next is a mystery  why were they killed who killed them and  why was a cyclist murdered alongside  them and after nearly a decade of  investigation  we don't really have any answers  if there was a message this week it was  this  the investigation continues  even after all this time  adam parsons sky news anna c
 

